            "value": [
              {
                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "<p>This file contains the semi-structured interview guide developed for the HL-EXURB project. The questionnaire was designed to explore the hybrid lifestyles of creative ex-urbanites and their connections to urban, rural, and digital spaces.</p><p>\n\nThe interview guide covers key thematic areas including:</p><p><ul>\n\n<li>motivations for relocation and lifestyle change\n</li><li>professional practices and digital forms of work\n</li><li>everyday life in rural settings\n</li><li>socio-ecological practices and values\n</li><li>interactions with local communities and forms of community-making\n</li></ul></p><p>\nInterviews were conducted with purposively selected participants who previously lived in urban areas and are currently engaged in creative, digital, or hybrid professional activities in a rural context.</p><p>\n\nThe guide follows a flexible structure, allowing for in-depth exploration of participants’ experiences while ensuring comparability across interviews.</p>"
                }
              }
            ]
